sks.   For more information, see Substitution Management.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-21\nValid as Of: 2025-05-21\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 809 ---\nComponent: Variant Configuration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Extensions Concept – Disable Buffering of Local Extension Calls\nDescription: In remote extension implementations, you can return response header Cache-Control: no-store to disable the call buffering of a custom pricing routine. Now it is also possible to disable the call buffering for local extensions by listing the JavaScript function name with the parameter caching: false in a manifest file.  See: Extension Guide for SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-21\nValid as Of: 2025-05-21\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 810 ---\nComponent: Variant Configuration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Production - Configurations API - Correct Response Status For Locking Configurations\nDescription: The endpoint\",2061\n88,\" to return the locked flag for a document.   The existing endpoint GET /pricing/documents will be enhanced to allow searching for locked documents.   See  API Definition and Development Guide for SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing - Pre-Production.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-16\nValid as Of: 2025-05-07\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 950 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: My Processes Application\nDescription: You can now use the My Processes application to view and track instances across processes based on your access rights. You can also configure the application to view the requests you have raised.See Use My Processes Application.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-07\nValid as Of: 2025-05-07\nVersion: Cloud\n\n\",2061\n370,\"--- Record 1581 ---\nComponent: Variant Configuration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Pre-Production – Configurations API – Read Single Characteristics\nDescription: There is a new endpoint called GET /api/v2/configurations/{configurationId}/items/{itemId}/characteristics used to read the details of one or more characteristics of an item.   Action: If the UI of the consuming application allows it, it is recommended to always read the configuration results during interactive configuration without the possible values of characteristics. This can be achieved by using the parameter $select omitting the parameter value possibleValue when creating or reading a configuration. Only when the user clicks on a UI element, like a dropdown list box, that requires to render the possible values on the UI, the possible values should be read for that characteristic using the new endpoint. This will improve performance especially when AVC Forwarding is enabled.   See: API Definition and Development Guide for SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing.\nAction: Recommended\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-12\nValid as Of: 2025-01-22\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1582 ---\nComponent: Variant Configuration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Staged Deployment Strategy\nDescription: There is a new staged deployment strategy for the Variant Configuration service starting with the 2502 release. New software releases used to be deployed to all customer tenants at the same time. We will continue to do that for our administration UI and our Administration service, but for the configuration and pricing services we will first deploy the 2502 release only to all non-productive tenants (including the partner tenants) on January 22, 2025 and only two weeks later, on February 5, 2025 we will also deploy it to the productive tenants.  Action: It is recommended to make yourself familiar with the release dates on our product page. Review the changes in the Pre-Production version of the documentation that will be published on January 22, and use the given two weeks to test the new release in your non-productive tenants and process the actions of the recommended or required changes that are announced here in the release notes.  See: Release Schedule and Dates.\nAction: Recommended\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-12\nValid as Of: 2025-01-22\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1583 ---\nComponent: Application for Data Replication and Administration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Advanced Actions - Remote Subscription Exception Display\nDescription: The update mechanism for displaying errors relating to the SDI DP Agent was not working properly. This led to instances in which the error was shown only for a few seconds. This issue has been corrected\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-12\nValid as Of: 2025-01-22\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1584 ---\nComponent: Application for Data Replication and Administration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Delta Replication Alert for SAP CALM\nDescription: The alert for a too high number of deltas is now also sent to SAP Cloud Application Lifecycle Monitoring – Integration Monitoring.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-12\nValid as Of: 2025-01-22\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1585 ---\nComponent: Cloud Integration for Data Services\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Documentation update only: Component for SAP Support Updated\nDescription: In the Help Center topic View Data in a Datastore, the component you should use when asking SAP Support to activate View Data functionality for you has been updated to LOD-HCI-DS-